        <JournalIssue><PubDate><Year>2023</Year><Month>Mar</Month></PubDate></JournalIssue></Journal>
      <ArticleTitle>Tranexamic acid in total knee arthroplasty: a systematic review and meta-analysis of randomized trials.</ArticleTitle>
      <Abstract>
        <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Blood loss after total knee arthroplasty often leads to transfusion.</AbstractText>
        <AbstractText Label="METHODS">We pooled 42 randomized controlled trials comparing tranexamic acid with placebo.</AbstractText>
        <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">Tranexamic acid reduced the risk of transfusion (relative risk 0.45, 95% CI 0.38 to 0.53) without increasing venous thromboembolism.</AbstractText>
        <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS">Tranexamic acid is effective and safe for reducing transfusion in knee arthroplasty.</AbstractText>
      </Abstract>
